# Deploy-ZIP exclusions (git archive honors export-ignore).
# This file documents a prior incident and quotes malware IOC strings;
# shipping it to a host triggers malware scanners (SiteGround, 2026-08-04).
# It stays in git; it must never ship in a deploy artifact.
docs/security-investigation-nlo-finance-redirect-2026-07-09.md export-ignore

# ⭐⭐ 1.19.343 (2026-08-31, `CYCLE173-LD-CONSENT-CHECKOUT`) — TWO ARTEFACT
#    DEFECTS THAT ONLY A BYTE DIFF AGAINST A LIVE ENVIRONMENT REVEALS.
#    Both were found by diffing the deployed staging theme against the
#    pre-deploy backup, not by reading the build command.
#
# 1. `assets/covers/` — 117 tracked cover-design source and proof files
#    (`*-source-v1.png`, `*-dark-proof-v1.jpg`). COUNTED, not estimated:
#    referenced by ZERO php/js/css in this theme, and present on NEITHER
#    environment — production and staging were both 610 files before this
#    release, and neither had this directory. A repo-built ZIP silently
#    added all 117 to staging.
#
#    ⛔ This is the SAME RULE `tools/` already lives under, in the same
#       spirit the RUNBOOK states it: ARTEFACTS DEPLOY, SOURCES DO NOT.
#       These are design masters, not runtime assets. Excluding them keeps
#       the deployed file set equal to what production actually runs, so a
#       post-deploy byte diff stays a usable instrument.
#
#    ⚠ If a cover image is ever genuinely needed at runtime, the fix is to
#      add THAT ONE optimised file somewhere served, not to delete this
#      line and ship 117 design masters onto a public web server.
assets/covers export-ignore

# ⛔ LINE ENDINGS IN THE DEPLOY ARTEFACT — READ THIS BEFORE BUILDING A ZIP.
#
# This repository is worked on a Windows box with `core.autocrlf=true`, so
# a plain `git archive` writes CRLF into every text file in the ZIP. Both
# live environments run LF (verified: `tr -cd '\r' < 404.php | wc -c`
# returns 0 on production, 2026-08-31).
#
# The consequence is not a broken site — PHP, JS, CSS and Markdown are all
# indifferent — it is that EVERY TEXT FILE IN THE THEME CHANGES BYTE-WISE
# ON DEPLOY. That destroys the one instrument that proves a release changed
# only what it claims to: on the first 1.19.343 staging deploy the raw diff
# reported ~250 files "differ" when the real number was 4.
#
# ⭐ THE FIX IS AT BUILD TIME, and the RUNBOOK carries it:
#       git -c core.autocrlf=false -c core.eol=lf archive …
#    It is deliberately NOT a `* text eol=lf` rule here, because that would
#    rewrite the working tree for every future checkout on this machine and
#    produce one enormous unrelated diff. The build flag is narrow and
#    affects only the artefact.
